version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-06-28
abstract: >
  agent.txtar is a portable, embeddable text block that tells AI agents what they
  need to know — about a person, project, org, or rules. Built on Go's txtar archive
  format, it bundles multiple virtual files inside a single plain-text block that can
  be pasted anywhere: a GitHub README, a blog sidebar, a social media bio, or served
  as a standalone file. Agents parse the structured manifest inside; humans just see
  readable text.
